<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amir Hamzah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tengku Amir Hamzah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">Amir</a> Hamzah was an Indonesian poet and a member of the royal family of the Langkat Sultanate in North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>. His collections Nyanyi Sunyi and Buah Rindu, written in Malay in the 1930s, made him the leading poet of the Pujangga Baru generation. He was killed in March 1946 during the social revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-sumatra">East Sumatra</a> and was later named a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amir-hamzah.jpg" alt="Amir Hamzah" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uncredited; restoration by Crisco 1492 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amir_Hamzah_portrait_edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
